skill: "story-pointing-calibration"
sections[3]:
  - "# story-pointing-calibration\n\nAnchor estimation to reference stories and detect drift. Use during backlog refinement, when velocity swings more than the control band between sprints, or when estimates from different contributors stop being comparable. Produces calibrated estimates with a recorded spread, not false precision.\n\nOwner: role-scrum-agile-coach (pod-build, product). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"reference story table reference-stories.toon (one per point value with measured effort); rolling velocity history last 6 sprints from sprint-metrics.toon; candidate items from grooming-log.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/product/estimation-session.toon with per-item point, spread and reference anchor; capacity band for the next sprint\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load reference-stories.toon and the last six sprints of velocity; compute the rolling capacity band (median plus/minus one mean absolute deviation) with run_command.\n2. For each candidate item, compare against the reference class closest in shape and size; name the anchor story in the record instead of quoting a bare number.\n3. Collect independent votes from contributing agents or the operator before any discussion; record the first-round spread.\n4. Flag anchoring drift: if an item's vote spread spans more than two point bands, stop and surface the disagreement instead of averaging it away.\n5. Re-vote only the flagged items after the shortest possible clarification; cap the session at two rounds per item.\n6. Verify each final estimate against the capacity band; if committed scope exceeds the band, mark the excess as carry-over candidates now, not after the sprint starts.\n7. Write estimation-session.toon with point, spread, anchor and dissents[] preserved; never collapse a recorded dissent into a silent average.\n8. Feed sprint-metrics.toon so the next velocity reading is comparable to this session's assumptions.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ncapacity band to sprint planning; metric assumptions to sprint-metrics.toon.\n"
